flowchart TD
    box_0(["Start"])
    box_1["Record the measured insertion depth values, the<br/>direction of deviation (too shallow or too deep),<br/>and the batch number. Collect five representative<br/>parts for reference."]
    box_2{"Is the insertion depth deviation consistent and in<br/>one direction (all too shallow or all too deep)?"}
    box_3["Complete the following steps: 1. Record insertion<br/>depth readings for ten consecutive parts. 2.<br/>Calculate the mean depth and compare against the<br/>nominal target. 3. Check whether the deviation is<br/>consistent or varies between parts."]
    box_4["If the depth deviation is random, check part to part<br/>dimensional variation in the batch. Sample five<br/>parts for dimensional measurement."]
    box_5{"Is the part material batch dimensionally within the<br/>specification for this product type?"}
    box_6["Measure the outer diameter and top surface geometry<br/>of five parts from the current batch and compare<br/>against the incoming material specification."]
    box_7["Reject the current batch as dimensionally non<br/>conforming. Reload from a batch with confirmed<br/>dimensional conformance. Create a non conformance<br/>record."]
    box_8{"Is the press depth setting (lower position setpoint)<br/>correct for this product type?"}
    box_9["Complete the following checks: 1. Read the lower<br/>position setpoint from the press depth parameter<br/>screen. 2. Compare the stored setpoint against the<br/>value on the validated process sheet. 3. Check<br/>whether the setpoint was changed since the last<br/>confirmed good run."]
    box_10["Adjust the press depth setting to the specified<br/>value for this product type and rerun a test<br/>pressing cycle. Verify the corrected depth."]
    box_11{"Is the pressing head making full, flat contact with<br/>the top surface of the part at the lower position?"}
    box_12["Jog the pressing head to the lower position and<br/>visually inspect the contact between the pressing<br/>head face and the part top surface. Check for tilt<br/>or partial contact."]
    box_13["Realign the pressing head perpendicular to the part<br/>axis and verify that full flat contact is achieved<br/>across the entire contact surface."]
    box_14{"Is the depth measurement gauge reading correctly<br/>(validated against the reference block)?"}
    box_15["Place the reference calibration block under the<br/>depth gauge and verify that the readout matches the<br/>reference block value within the specified gauge<br/>tolerance."]
    box_16["Rezero the depth gauge using the reference block and<br/>repeat the calibration check. Replace the depth<br/>gauge if the offset exceeds the acceptable<br/>correction range."]
    box_17{"Is the insertion depth within specification after<br/>all corrections?"}
    box_18["Escalate to the maintenance team: insertion depth is<br/>outside specification despite all standard<br/>corrective actions; inspect the pressing station<br/>mechanical stops and actuator condition."]
    box_19["Record corrective actions and the verified insertion<br/>depth measurements in the quality log. Notify<br/>quality assurance team."]
    box_20(["End, notify quality assurance team."])
    box_21{"Is the insertion depth deviation large enough to<br/>indicate a part to fixture mismatch or a tooling<br/>failure that would cause damaged parts if production<br/>continues?"}
    box_22(["End, production stopped immediately: insertion depth<br/>deviation critical, quarantine all parts produced<br/>since last good measurement and escalate to process<br/>engineer"])

